-- an equation that does not hold is rejected: neither eqw≡weq nor a constant line proves eqw = wlt
-- words are exact: past 2^64 a word cell holds its digits
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- guarded recursion
-- ▸ κ A is an A one tick of the clock κ later: (α : Tick κ) → A. A tick is bound by λ and given by
-- application; a function applied to a tick α uses nothing bound after α (the checker's
-- timelessness rule), so a later value is never used now. Clocks are quantified by Π over Clock;
-- κ0 is the closed clock.
next : {l : Level} {κ : Clock} {A : Type l} → A → ▸ κ A
next a = λ α → a
